+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+As the contract stands, `deposit()` **cannot succeed against the real USDT at
+`0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`**. Every deposit reverts. The vault
+would be a bricked contract on mainnet from block one. That alone is a ship-blocker,
+and it is proved below against the live chain.
+
+Behind that, the accounting model has three further defects that each destroy or
+misdirect user money once the first one is fixed: the vault pays out **zero Aave
+interest** (the yield is permanently unclaimable), the withdrawal fee is **destroyed
+rather than redistributed** as the README promises, and the owner can **seize an
+incoming deposit** through an unbounded `depositFeeBps`.
+
+Nothing under `src/` was modified. All new work is in `test/review/`.
+
+---
+
+## Why the suite is green
+
+The 39 passing tests are real, and the coverage number is real:
+
+```
+$ forge coverage --match-path 'test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol'
+| File                                 | % Lines         | % Statements    | % Branches    | % Funcs         |
+| src/UsdtYieldVault.sol               | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57)  | 85.71% (6/7)  | 100.00% (11/11) |
+```
+
+They are green because of what they are pointed at, not because the code is correct.
+Two properties of `test/mocks/` do all the work:
+
+1. `MockUSDT` is a stock OpenZeppelin `ERC20`. It returns `bool` from `approve`,
+   has no transfer fee, and has no blacklist. **The deployed USDT has none of
+   those properties.** Line coverage of `usdt.approve(...)` is 100% and the line
+   is nevertheless guaranteed to revert in production.
+2. `MockAavePool` mints aTokens 1:1 and never accrues interest. The vault is a
+   *yield* vault whose test double pays no yield, so no test can observe that the
+   yield never reaches anybody.
+
+Coverage measures which lines ran. It does not measure whether the environment
+those lines ran in resembles mainnet. Here it did not.
+
+---
+
+## What I added
+
+| File | What it is |
+| --- | --- |
+| `test/review/RealisticUSDT.sol` | Transcription of the deployed TetherToken semantics: no return values, the non-zero→non-zero `approve` guard, the `basisPointsRate` transfer fee, the blacklist. |
+| `test/review/FeeSwitchUSDT.sol` | USDT with the transfer fee switched on but standard `bool` returns — only so that F-7 can be reached past F-1. |
+| `test/review/YieldingAavePool.sol` | Aave V3 stand-in with a rebasing aToken (liquidity index) and the real pool's `amount != 0` validation. |
+| `test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol` | Property tests. `test_Spec_*` state a property the vault must hold and **fail**. `test_Evidence_*` / `test_Exploit_*` **pass** and pin down the broken behaviour. |
+| `test/review/VaultInvariants.t.sol` | Stateful invariants over random deposit / withdraw / interest sequences. |
+| `test/review/ForkMainnet.t.sol` | Runs the vault against the real USDT, the real Aave V3 pool and the real aUSDT on a mainnet fork. |
+
+Reproduce everything:
