+## Findings
+
+| # | Severity | Finding |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| F-1 | **Critical** | `deposit()` always reverts against the real USDT — the vault is inoperable on mainnet |
+| F-2 | **Critical** | Unbounded `depositFeeBps` lets the owner front-run and seize an incoming deposit |
+| F-3 | **High** | All Aave interest is unclaimable — the vault pays no yield and locks it forever |
+| F-4 | **High** | The withdrawal fee is destroyed, not redistributed as documented |
+| F-5 | **High** | `pause()` blocks `withdraw()`, and `renounceOwnership()` can make that permanent |
+| F-6 | Medium | `setDepositFee(> 10_000)` bricks all deposits with an arithmetic panic |
+| F-7 | Medium | If Tether re-enables its transfer fee, deposits revert |
+| F-8 | Low | `totalAssetsStored` overstates redeemable aUSDT because of Aave's index rounding |
+| F-9 | Low | Dust withdrawals revert inside Aave's `amount != 0` check |
+
