+### F-3 — High — all Aave interest is unclaimable
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:143-145`
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return totalAssetsStored;
+}
+```
+
+`totalAssetsStored` only ever moves by the nominal amounts passed to `deposit` and
+`withdraw`. It never reads `aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`. aUSDT is a rebasing
+token: the vault's balance grows as Aave accrues interest, and the vault's pricing
+is blind to all of it. The share price cannot rise. Depositors receive **exactly
+their principal minus fees**, and the interest they earned stays behind.
+
+The `aUsdt` immutable is declared at line 41, set in the constructor, and then
+never read anywhere in the contract. Nothing in the vault has any idea how much
+aUSDT it actually holds.
+
+**Evidence:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Spec_AaveInterestReachesDepositors -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[FAIL: alice must earn the Aave interest: 1000000000 !~= 1100000000 (max delta: 1000000, real delta: 100000000)] test_Spec_AaveInterestReachesDepositors() (gas: 2456794)
+Logs:
+  aUSDT held by vault      : 1100000000
+  vault.totalAssets()      : 1000000000
+  alice balanceOfUnderlying: 1000000000
+```
+
+The vault holds 1,100 USDT of aUSDT. It reports 1,000. Alice — the only depositor,
+who earned all 100 USDT of it — can claim 1,000.
+
+Where the interest goes:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Evidence_InterestIsIgnoredByAccounting -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[PASS] test_Evidence_InterestIsIgnoredByAccounting() (gas: 2362500)
+Suite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 799.29µs (239.71µs CPU time)
+```
+
+That test asserts the end state exactly: after Alice's full exit, `totalShares == 0`
+and the vault still holds `103e6` aUSDT — 100 USDT of interest plus her 3 USDT exit
+fee. There is no sweep function, no rescue function, and no share left that could
+ever price it in. It is gone.
+
+This is the product, not an edge case. A yield vault that returns no yield is
+mis-sold to every depositor.
+
+**Fix.** Delete `totalAssetsStored` and derive value from the position:
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+}
+```
+
+with `convertToShares` / `convertToAssets` reading `totalAssets()`. Because
+`aUsdt` is a rebasing aToken and the vault holds no idle USDT, its balance is the
+correct and complete measure of the position, so interest lands in the share price
+automatically. Two consequences to handle in the same change:
+
+- Balance-based pricing reopens the classic first-depositor donation attack that
+  the storage-based design happens to be immune to (see "What holds", below).
+  Mint a small amount of dead shares to `address(0)` on the first deposit, or seed
+  the vault at deployment, or use OpenZeppelin's ERC4626 virtual-offset approach.
+- `withdraw` must then request `grossAssets`, not `netAssets`, from Aave — see F-4.
+
+The cleanest route is to inherit `ERC4626` and override `totalAssets()`. It gets
+the rounding directions, the inflation defence, and a standard interface that
+integrators already understand.
+
