+### F-5 — High — `pause()` freezes withdrawals, and it can be made permanent
+
+`withdraw()` carries `whenNotPaused` (line 107). Pausing therefore traps depositor
+funds rather than protecting them. `Ownable` is inherited without overriding
+`renounceOwnership()`, so a compromised or careless owner can pause and then
+renounce, and there is nobody left who can ever unpause.
+
+**Evidence:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Spec_DepositorsCanExitWhilePaused -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[FAIL: EnforcedPause()] test_Spec_DepositorsCanExitWhilePaused() (gas: 2444849)
+```
+
+The test pauses, calls `renounceOwnership()` (which succeeds — `vault.owner()`
+becomes `address(0)`), and then asserts Alice can get her money out. She cannot.
+`test_Evidence_PauseThenRenounceFreezesFundsForever` **passes**, asserting the
+`EnforcedPause()` revert as the permanent end state.
+
+**Fix.**
+- Remove `whenNotPaused` from `withdraw()`. A pause should stop money going in,
+  never stop money coming out. If you need an emergency stop on exits too, make it
+  a separate, time-limited switch with an on-chain expiry.
+- Override `renounceOwnership()` to revert, or move ownership to a multisig with a
+  timelock. As written, one transaction from the owner key permanently destroys
+  every deposit.
+
