+
+### F-6 — Medium — a fee above 100% bricks deposits
+
+`setDepositFee` accepts any `uint256`. At `10_001`, `fee > amount` and line 88
+(`amount - fee`) panics on underflow. Every deposit reverts until the owner
+notices and fixes it.
+
+**Evidence:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Spec_DepositSurvivesAnyOwnerFeeSetting -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[FAIL: panic: arithmetic underflow or overflow (0x11)] test_Spec_DepositSurvivesAnyOwnerFeeSetting() (gas: 2246580)
+```
+
+`test_Evidence_FeeAbove100PercentPanics` **passes**, asserting
+`stdError.arithmeticError` precisely.
+
+**Fix.** Same cap as F-2 (`MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS`). This finding disappears once F-2
+is fixed; it is listed separately because it is the failure mode you get from a fat
+finger rather than from malice, and because an unhandled panic is a worse UX than a
+named error.
+
