+
+### F-7 — Medium — USDT's transfer fee would brick deposits
+
+The deployed USDT still contains Tether's `basisPointsRate` / `maximumFee`
+mechanism, settable by Tether's owner via `setParams` up to 20 bps capped at 50 USDT.
+It is currently zero:
+
+```
+$ cast call 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7 "basisPointsRate()(uint256)" --rpc-url https://eth.drpc.org
+0
+$ cast call 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7 "maximumFee()(uint256)" --rpc-url https://eth.drpc.org
+0
+```
+
+If it is ever turned on, `deposit` breaks: the vault receives `amount - fee` at
+line 93 but then tries to supply the full `amount` at line 95, and `totalAssetsStored`
+would credit the full `amount` too.
+
+**Evidence** (using `FeeSwitchUSDT`, which is USDT's fee logic with standard `bool`
+returns — the bool returns are not realistic and exist only so this defect can be
+reached past F-1):
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Spec_DepositWorksWhenUsdtChargesTransferFee -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[FAIL: ERC20InsufficientBalance(0xF62849F9A0B5Bf2913b396098F7c7019b51A820a, 998000000 [9.98e8], 999000000 [9.99e8])] test_Spec_DepositWorksWhenUsdtChargesTransferFee() (gas: 2393935)
+```
+
+Deposits revert outright. That is the benign outcome; it is only benign because
+the amount supplied and the amount credited happen to be the same variable. Any
+future refactor that decouples them turns this into silent over-crediting.
+
+**Fix.** Measure what actually arrived:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 balanceBefore = usdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+usdt.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+uint256 received = usdt.balanceOf(address(this)) - balanceBefore;
+```
+
+and use `received` for the supply, the fee and the share maths. This is standard
+practice for any vault that accepts USDT and costs one extra `balanceOf`.
+
+I am flagging this as Medium rather than Low specifically because the underlying is
+USDT. The fee switch is live code on a token whose parameters are outside your
+control, and "it is set to zero today" is not a property you can rely on for a
+contract with no upgrade path.
+
+---
+
+### F-8 — Low — `totalAssetsStored` can exceed the redeemable aUSDT
+
+Aave divides the supplied amount by the reserve's liquidity index and rounds down,
+so supplying `X` credits at most `X` aTokens and usually `X - 1`. `deposit` credits
+`totalAssetsStored` the full nominal `amount`. The vault's books therefore drift
+above what Aave will actually pay out, by up to one base unit per deposit.
+
+**Evidence — on the real Aave V3 pool:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Fork_Evidence_AaveCreditsLessThanSupplied --fork-url https://eth.drpc.org --fork-block-number 25845000 -vv
+
+[PASS] test_Fork_Evidence_AaveCreditsLessThanSupplied() (gas: 403793)
+Logs:
+  USDT supplied to Aave      : 1000000000
+  aUSDT credited by Aave     : 999999999
+  shortfall the vault records: 1
+```
+
+**Evidence — the invariant catches the resulting under-collateralisation:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/review/VaultInvariants.t.sol'
+
+[FAIL: assertion failed: 45152190670 < 45152190671]
+	[Sequence] (original: 2, shrunk: 2)
+		sender=0x00000000000000000000000000000000000013d0 addr=[test/review/VaultInvariants.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=accrueInterest(uint256) args=[21691949879437928403120091854919001864570428592072130319780848770032031 [2.169e70]]
+		sender=0xBf9cE6F3b840b0A48e63B689e10b95B9D50b0b1d addr=[test/review/VaultInvariants.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=deposit(uint256,uint256) args=[740129612370620938006214361024798427519776 [7.401e41], 36607463840129869235610120906332 [3.66e31]]
+ invariant_A_TrackedAssetsAreActuallyRedeemable() (runs: 3, calls: 1500, reverts: 0)
+```
+
+Held aUSDT `45152190670` against tracked `45152190671`: the vault claims one base
+unit more than it can pay.
+
+**Honest severity.** This is Low on its own. The 0.3% withdrawal fee leaves far more
+surplus behind (F-4) than the rounding removes, so in practice the surplus dominates
+and no withdrawal fails because of this. `testFuzz_SolventWhenNoInterestAccrues`
+**passes**, confirming the vault stays over-collateralised on the no-interest path.
+I am reporting it because it shows the underlying problem cleanly: `totalAssetsStored`
+is a *guess* at the position, kept in sync by hand, and it is already wrong on the
+very first deposit. It stops being a guess the moment F-3's fix reads the aToken
+balance instead — which is why F-8 needs no separate fix.
+
+---
+
+### F-9 — Low — dust withdrawals revert inside Aave
+
+A share amount small enough that `convertToAssets` floors to 0 produces
+`netAssets == 0`, and Aave V3's `validateWithdraw` rejects a zero amount
+(`Errors.INVALID_AMOUNT`, code `26`).
+
+**Evidence:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Spec_DustWithdrawDoesNotRevertInAave -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[FAIL: 26] test_Spec_DustWithdrawDoesNotRevertInAave() (gas: 2441389)
+```
+
+`26` is Aave's `INVALID_AMOUNT`. The state change reverts with it, so no funds are
+lost — but note that `test/mocks/MockAavePool` does **not** perform this check, so
+under the project's own mock the same call burns the shares and pays out nothing.
+The suite would never have shown you either behaviour.
+
+**Fix.** Revert early in `withdraw()` with a named error when `netAssets == 0`,
+so callers get a legible failure instead of an Aave error code.
+
+---
+
+## What holds
+
+Recorded so this reads as a review and not a list of complaints. These are checks
+I ran that the contract passes:
+
+- **No first-depositor share-inflation attack.** Because pricing reads
+  `totalAssetsStored` rather than a token balance, donating aUSDT directly to the
+  vault does not move the share price. `test_DonationCannotInflateSharePrice`
+  passes: a 10,000 USDT donation against a 1 USDT first deposit is invisible to
+  pricing, and the next depositor still mints correctly. **This immunity is a side
+  effect of the bug in F-3 and you will lose it when you fix F-3** — put the
+  inflation defence in at the same time.
+- **No rounding leak on a round trip.** `testFuzz_RoundTripNeverProfits` (256 runs)
+  confirms deposit-then-withdraw never returns more than it took in.
+- **Share accounting is internally consistent.** `invariant_B_SharesSumToTotalShares`
+  holds over 128,000 calls of randomised deposits, withdrawals and interest accrual.
+- **`nonReentrant` and `whenNotPaused` are on both state-changing entry points**, and
+  `SafeERC20` is used for the transfers. USDT has no transfer hooks, so the ordering
+  of the external calls in `deposit` is not exploitable.
+- **`totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets` cannot underflow.** `grossAssets` is
+  `shares * stored / totalShares` with `shares <= totalShares`, so it is bounded by
+  `stored`; and `totalAssetsStored` cannot reach zero while shares remain
+  outstanding, so `convertToShares` cannot divide by zero. I checked this
+  specifically because it would have been a live denial-of-service.
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test 'testFuzz_|test_DonationCannotInflate'
+
+Ran 3 tests for test/review/UsdtYieldVaultSpec.t.sol:UsdtYieldVaultSpecTest
+[PASS] testFuzz_RoundTripNeverProfits(uint96) (runs: 256, μ: 2352809, ~: 2352945)
+[PASS] testFuzz_SolventWhenNoInterestAccrues(uint96,uint96) (runs: 256, μ: 2435984, ~: 2436227)
+[PASS] test_DonationCannotInflateSharePrice() (gas: 2473015)
+Suite result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 49.41ms (87.27ms CPU time)
+```
+
+The existing suite is untouched and still green:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol'
+Suite result: ok. 39 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 1.62ms (4.34ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 151.77ms (1.62ms CPU time): 39 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (39 total tests)
+```
+
+---
+
+## Informational
+
+Not demonstrated with failing tests; worth fixing in the same pass.
+
+- **`aUsdt` is dead storage.** Declared at line 41, assigned in the constructor,
+  never read. Fixing F-3 gives it a job.
+- **No zero-address validation in the constructor.** `_usdt`, `_aUsdt` and
+  `_aavePool` are all accepted as `address(0)`, and all three are `immutable`, so a
+  deployment typo is unrecoverable. Add `require` checks, and assert
+  `IAToken(_aUsdt).UNDERLYING_ASSET_ADDRESS() == _usdt`.
+- **No initial fee validation.** `_depositFeeBps` bypasses whatever cap you add to
+  `setDepositFee`.
+- **Shares are not transferable and the vault is not ERC4626.** No `transfer`, no
+  approvals, no `previewDeposit` / `maxWithdraw`. Integrators cannot compose with
+  it, and depositors cannot move a position without a full exit through the fee.
+  Inheriting `ERC4626` addresses this and F-3 together.
+- **No rescue path.** Any token sent to the vault by mistake — including aUSDT — is
+  permanently stuck.
+- **USDT blacklisting.** If Tether blacklists the vault address, every withdrawal
+  reverts and every deposit reverts. Nothing can be done about that in the contract,
+  but it belongs in the risk disclosure.
+- **Aave availability.** If the USDT reserve is paused or frozen, or the supply cap
+  is reached, `deposit` reverts; if utilisation is at 100%, `withdraw` reverts and
+  depositors cannot exit until borrowers repay. Worth monitoring and disclosing.
+- **The deposit fee is a no-op for a sole depositor**, who pays it to themselves.
+  Harmless, but the fee schedule does not do what its name suggests until there is
+  a second depositor.
+
+---
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Do not deploy on Monday. F-1 alone means the contract does not function on mainnet,
+and it would have been caught by a single fork test against the address already
+written in your README. F-2 through F-5 mean that once F-1 is fixed, the contract
+loses or misdirects real money.
+
+The specific thing I would change about how this was tested: the mocks in
+`test/mocks/` encode the token and the money market you *wish* you were integrating
+with, and 100% coverage against them proves only internal self-consistency. A
+mainnet fork test against `0xdAC17F9...` and `0x87870Bca...` — five lines of setup —
+would have turned the whole suite red before any of this review started.
+
+After the fixes, I would want to see: the fork tests in `test/review/ForkMainnet.t.sol`
+green, `invariant_C` and `invariant_D` green, an added invariant that the sum of all
+depositor claims equals `aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`, and an external audit
+before real deposits.
